          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "व्यसनम् — vyasanam — \"a vice; an addiction\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "द्यूतम् एकं व्यसनम् अस्ति। dyūtam ekaṃ vyasanam asti. Gambling is a vice."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "व्यसनम् (vyasanam) is built from vi and the root √as, \"to throw\": throwing oneself into a thing; MW gives \"attachment or addiction to\" and \"evil passion, vice\" (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
